SELECT define_provision($q$ICC_CITY_PLAN_2025@2026-07-01$q$, $q$9.3.7.3 Table 9.3.7.3.2 (Benchmarks for Assessable Development), PO2.2 / AO2.2.1 / AO2.2.2$q$, 'PERFORMANCE_OUTCOME', $q$PO2.2
Dwelling houses and Dual occupancies reflect the established or desired built character of the locality and maintain:
access to views, prevailing breezes and natural light; and
amenity on adjoining lots, by providing separation from adjoining Dwellings to the side and rear of the development.
AO2.2.1
Side boundary setbacks meet the requirements of Queensland Development Code MP1.1, MP1.2 or MP1.3 (as relevant) unless:
in the New Suburban precinct, where side boundaries are as per MP1.1, MP1.2 and MP1.3 with a built to boundary setback for a garage on one side, up to a length of 9m, or
in the Rural zone, where side boundary setbacks are a minimum of 20m.
AO2.2.2
A built to boundary or dividing wall is not:
within 900mm of a window or wall, or
within 1500mm of a window to a habitable room*.
* Windows or walls that are already constructed, or that are part of an existing approval.$q$, 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', $q$ruleId 35432$q$, NULL, $q$Dwelling House and Dual Occupancy Code$q$, NULL, $q$https://ipswich.isoplan.com.au/eplan/rules/0/404/0/0/0/203 (JSON: https://ipswich.isoplan.com.au/eplan/api/l/r/404/0/false/30-Jun-2026/false)$q$, $q$SC1.2 'Setback': 'the shortest distance, measured horizontally, between the outermost projection of the building or structure to the vertical projection of the boundary of the lot'. Where the outcome defers to QDC MP1.1/MP1.2/MP1.3 the QDC measurement rules apply.$q$, $q$dh_po2_2_side_rear_separation_assessable$q$);
