SELECT define_provision($q$ICC_CITY_PLAN_2025@2026-07-01$q$, $q$8.2.3.3 Table 8.2.3.3.1 (Benchmarks for ADSR), RO1.1$q$, 'ACCEPTED_DEVELOPMENT_REQUIREMENT', $q$Class 10 buildings and structures (excluding fencing, gates and retaining walls)
RO1.1
When building in Area A to the rear of the main building (refer to Figure 8.2.3.3.20.1) the following applies:
may include open and enclosed Class 10 buildings and structures, including car accommodation, sheds, pools and other buildings and structures;
is detached from the main building; and
has a gross floor area no greater than 50% of the existing main building.$q$, 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', $q$ruleId 14489$q$, NULL, $q$Character Places and Areas Overlay Code$q$, NULL, $q$https://ipswich.isoplan.com.au/eplan/rules/0/332/0/0/0/203 (JSON: https://ipswich.isoplan.com.au/eplan/api/l/r/332/0/false/30-Jun-2026/false)$q$, $q$Areas A-D are shown on Figure 8.2.3.3.20.1 (image not extracted).$q$, $q$char_ro1_1_class10_rear_area_a$q$);
SELECT define_rule($q${"rule_id": "ICC.char_ro1_1_class10_rear_area_a", "instrument_version": "ICC_CITY_PLAN_2025@2026-07-01", "topic": "OUTBUILDING.SIZE", "title": "8.2.3.3 Table 8.2.3.3.1 (Benchmarks for ADSR), RO1.1", "role": "REQUIREMENT", "regime": "PLANNING", "enforceability": "DEEMED_TO_COMPLY", "provision_kind": "ACCEPTED_DEVELOPMENT_REQUIREMENT", "measurement": "SCHEME_OUTBUILDING_SIZE", "operator": "<=", "value": 50, "unit": "% of existing main building GFA", "on_noncompliance": "PLANNING_APPROVAL_REQUIRED", "effective_from": "2026-07-01", "verification": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM", "automatable": false, "scopes": [{"level": "LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "lg": "IPSWICH"}, {"level": "OVERLAY", "overlay": "ICC:OV:OV3_CHARACTER_PLACES_AND_AREAS_OVERLAY"}, {"level": "OVERLAY", "overlay": "ICC:OV:OV3_CHARACTER_PLACES_AND_AREAS_OVERLAY"}], "subjects": ["ANY"], "sources": [{"key": "char_ro1_1_class10_rear_area_a", "role": "PRIMARY"}], "interpretation_notes": "AUTO-IMPORTED (draft). Extracted structure: {\"parameter\": \"GFA of class 10 building in Area A (rear of main building)\", \"operator\": \"<=\", \"value\": 50, \"unit\": \"% of existing main building GFA\", \"conditions\": [\"Area A to the rear of the main building (Figure 8.2.3.3.20.1)\", \"detached from main building\"], \"exceptions\": [], \"formula_text\": \"class10_GFA <= 0.5 * main_building_GFA\"}\nStructure scope 'Class 10 buildings and structures (excluding fencing, gates and retaining walls) incl. car accommodation, sheds, pools' mapped by keyword to ['ANY']\nAlternative provision to QDC/QHC: NO\nResearcher notes: Building works in a Local Character Area are ADSR against this code (Table 5.9.3); non-compliance makes them code assessable."}$q$::jsonb);
UPDATE rule_versions SET status = 'DRAFT' WHERE rule_version_id = $q$ICC.char_ro1_1_class10_rear_area_a@2026-07-01$q$;
SELECT define_provision($q$ICC_CITY_PLAN_2025@2026-07-01$q$, $q$8.2.3.3 Table 8.2.3.3.1 (Benchmarks for ADSR), RO1.2$q$, 'ACCEPTED_DEVELOPMENT_REQUIREMENT', $q$RO1.2
Open Class 10 buildings and structures, including car accommodation may also be located to the side of the main building in Area B (refer to Figure 8.2.3.3.20.1) where taking a form that:
is detached from the main building;
is open or battened where facing the street or public realm;
is in alignment with or set back behind the line of the internal frontage verandah wall;
is a maximum of 6 metres wide;
where including a roof:
has a roof pitch which is a minimum of 15 degrees;
has a gable or hip roof form;
has roof overhangs that are a minimum of 300mm on all sides;
contains corrugated metal roofing material or matches the roofing material used on the main building; and
has a quad gutter profile or matches the gutter profile used on the main building;
has 100mm x 100mm support posts (timber or steel); and
where enclosed:
with timber battens, maintaining a minimum 30% transparency by providing spacing between each batten;
doors facing the street (swing, panel lift or tilt) maintain a minimum 30% transparency by providing spacing between each batten; and
enclosed spaces are located at the rear of the building or structure (refer to Figure 8.2.3.3.20.2, Figure K) and use horizontal cladding to match existing buildings on site.$q$, 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', $q$ruleId 14489$q$, NULL, $q$Character Places and Areas Overlay Code$q$, NULL, $q$https://ipswich.isoplan.com.au/eplan/rules/0/332/0/0/0/203 (JSON: https://ipswich.isoplan.com.au/eplan/api/l/r/332/0/false/30-Jun-2026/false)$q$, $q$Siting is relative to the main building verandah wall line, not a numeric boundary setback.$q$, $q$char_ro1_2_class10_side_area_b$q$);
SELECT define_rule($q${"rule_id": "ICC.char_ro1_2_class10_side_area_b", "instrument_version": "ICC_CITY_PLAN_2025@2026-07-01", "topic": "GARAGE.FRONTAGE", "title": "8.2.3.3 Table 8.2.3.3.1 (Benchmarks for ADSR), RO1.2", "role": "REQUIREMENT", "regime": "PLANNING", "enforceability": "DEEMED_TO_COMPLY", "provision_kind": "ACCEPTED_DEVELOPMENT_REQUIREMENT", "measurement": "SCHEME_GARAGE_CARPORT", "operator": "<=", "value": 6, "unit": "m", "on_noncompliance": "PLANNING_APPROVAL_REQUIRED", "effective_from": "2026-07-01", "verification": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM", "automatable": false, "scopes": [{"level": "LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "lg": "IPSWICH"}, {"level": "OVERLAY", "overlay": "ICC:OV:OV3_CHARACTER_PLACES_AND_AREAS_OVERLAY"}, {"level": "OVERLAY", "overlay": "ICC:OV:OV3_CHARACTER_PLACES_AND_AREAS_OVERLAY"}], "subjects": ["CLASS_10A", "CLASS_1"], "sources": [{"key": "char_ro1_2_class10_side_area_b", "role": "PRIMARY"}], "interpretation_notes": "AUTO-IMPORTED (draft). Extracted structure: {\"parameter\": \"width of open class 10 structure in Area B\", \"operator\": \"<=\", \"value\": 6, \"unit\": \"m\", \"conditions\": [\"detached\", \"open or battened facing street\", \"in alignment with or set back behind the internal frontage verandah wall line\", \"roof pitch >=15 deg, gable/hip, overhangs >=300mm\", \"100x100mm posts\", \"battens >=30% transparency if enclosed\"], \"exceptions\": [], \"formula_text\": null}\nStructure scope 'Open class 10 buildings/structures incl. car accommodation beside the main building (Area B)' mapped by keyword to ['CLASS_10A', 'CLASS_1']\nAlternative provision to QDC/QHC: NO"}$q$::jsonb);
UPDATE rule_versions SET status = 'DRAFT' WHERE rule_version_id = $q$ICC.char_ro1_2_class10_side_area_b@2026-07-01$q$;
SELECT define_provision($q$ICC_CITY_PLAN_2025@2026-07-01$q$, $q$8.2.3.3 Table 8.2.3.3.1 (Benchmarks for ADSR), RO1.3$q$, 'ACCEPTED_DEVELOPMENT_REQUIREMENT', $q$RO1.3
Where the side setbacks are less than 3 metres and access to the side or rear of an existing dwelling is not possible due to existing dwelling placement, a single carport can be erected between the dwelling and the primary street alignment in Area C in a location that minimises obscuring the view of the character dwelling (refer to Figure 8.2.3.3.20.1) where taking a form that:
is detached from the main building;
is a maximum of 3.6 metres wide and 6 metres long;
has a roof pitch which matches the main building’s predominant roof pitch;
has roof overhangs on all sides that are a minimum of 300mm;
has a gable or hip roof form;
has 100mm x 100mm support posts (timber or steel);
corrugated metal roofing material or matches the roofing material used on the main building;
has a quad gutter profile or matches the gutter profile used on the main building; and
the carport may be enclosed using:
timber battens, maintaining a minimum 30% transparency by providing spacing between each batten; and
doors facing the street (swing, panel lift or tilt) maintain a minimum 30% transparency by providing spacing between each timber batten.$q$, 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', $q$ruleId 14489$q$, NULL, $q$Character Places and Areas Overlay Code$q$, NULL, $q$https://ipswich.isoplan.com.au/eplan/rules/0/332/0/0/0/203 (JSON: https://ipswich.isoplan.com.au/eplan/api/l/r/332/0/false/30-Jun-2026/false)$q$, $q$No numeric front setback stated for the carport.$q$, $q$char_ro1_3_carport_front_area_c$q$);
