UPDATE rule_versions SET status = 'DRAFT' WHERE rule_version_id = $q$ICC.char_ro1_3_carport_front_area_c@2026-07-01$q$;
SELECT define_provision($q$ICC_CITY_PLAN_2025@2026-07-01$q$, $q$8.2.3.3 Table 8.2.3.3.1 (Benchmarks for ADSR), RO1.4$q$, 'ACCEPTED_DEVELOPMENT_REQUIREMENT', $q$RO1.4
On a secondary frontage of a corner site (refer to Area D on Figure 8.2.3.3.20.1) open car accommodation may also be located where taking a form that:
is detached from the main building;
is a single or double width carport detached from the main building;
is a single gable for single carports;
for double carports, provide a pair of gabled or hipped roofs of equal width facing the secondary frontage (refer Figure 8.2.3.3.20.2, Figures B, F & G);
is a maximum of 6 metres wide and 6 metres long;
has a roof pitch which matches the main building’s predominant roof pitch;
provides roof overhangs on all sides that are a minimum of 300mm;
has 100mm x 100mm support posts (timber or steel);
provides corrugated metal roofing material or matches the roofing material used on the main building; and
has a quad gutter profile or matches the gutter profile used on the main building.$q$, 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', $q$ruleId 14489$q$, NULL, $q$Character Places and Areas Overlay Code$q$, NULL, $q$https://ipswich.isoplan.com.au/eplan/rules/0/332/0/0/0/203 (JSON: https://ipswich.isoplan.com.au/eplan/api/l/r/332/0/false/30-Jun-2026/false)$q$, $q$No numeric secondary-frontage setback stated.$q$, $q$char_ro1_4_carport_secondary_frontage_area_d$q$);
SELECT define_rule($q${"rule_id": "ICC.char_ro1_4_carport_secondary_frontage_area_d", "instrument_version": "ICC_CITY_PLAN_2025@2026-07-01", "topic": "SETBACK.SECONDARY_ROAD", "title": "8.2.3.3 Table 8.2.3.3.1 (Benchmarks for ADSR), RO1.4", "role": "REQUIREMENT", "regime": "PLANNING", "enforceability": "DEEMED_TO_COMPLY", "provision_kind": "ACCEPTED_DEVELOPMENT_REQUIREMENT", "measurement": "SCHEME_SETBACK_SECONDARY_FRONTAGE", "operator": "<=", "value": 6, "unit": "m", "on_noncompliance": "PLANNING_APPROVAL_REQUIRED", "effective_from": "2026-07-01", "verification": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM", "automatable": false, "scopes": [{"level": "LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "lg": "IPSWICH"}, {"level": "OVERLAY", "overlay": "ICC:OV:OV3_CHARACTER_PLACES_AND_AREAS_OVERLAY"}, {"level": "OVERLAY", "overlay": "ICC:OV:OV3_CHARACTER_PLACES_AND_AREAS_OVERLAY"}], "subjects": ["ANY"], "sources": [{"key": "char_ro1_4_carport_secondary_frontage_area_d", "role": "PRIMARY"}], "interpretation_notes": "AUTO-IMPORTED (draft). Extracted structure: {\"parameter\": \"carport dimensions on secondary frontage\", \"operator\": \"<=\", \"value\": 6, \"unit\": \"m\", \"conditions\": [\"corner site, Area D\", \"detached single or double carport\", \"max 6m wide and 6m long\"], \"exceptions\": [], \"formula_text\": \"width<=6m AND length<=6m\"}\nStructure scope 'open car accommodation on the secondary frontage of a corner site (Area D)' mapped by keyword to ['ANY'] (default)\nAlternative provision to QDC/QHC: NO"}$q$::jsonb);
UPDATE rule_versions SET status = 'DRAFT' WHERE rule_version_id = $q$ICC.char_ro1_4_carport_secondary_frontage_area_d@2026-07-01$q$;
SELECT define_provision($q$ICC_CITY_PLAN_2025@2026-07-01$q$, $q$8.2.3.3 Table 8.2.3.3.2 (Benchmarks for Assessable Development), PO7.2 / AO7.2$q$, 'ACCEPTABLE_OUTCOME', $q$PO7.2
New buildings or extensions to existing buildings contribute to the rhythm of the siting and spacing of buildings in the street, particularly where the siting and spacing pattern is highly regular.
AO7.2
New buildings are setback from the street an equal or greater distance than adjacent character buildings;
New buildings maintain a consistent spacing and harmonious rhythm (refer to Figure 8.2.3.3.3.3);
Where there is no character building or character place for setback reference, or a discordant rhythm exists new buildings are setback to comply with the specific outcomes for each zone;
New buildings or extensions to existing buildings are not constructed in front of the building alignment of existing character buildings;
New buildings, or extensions to existing buildings, ensure the distance between the boundary and the side external wall reflect the ratio of built form to open space which is similar to other character buildings in the street; and
New buildings are built to the property boundary where:
adjoining character buildings are constructed to the property boundary; and
the new building complies with the performance outcomes for the relevant zones.$q$, 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', $q$ruleId 14500$q$, NULL, $q$Character Places and Areas Overlay Code$q$, NULL, $q$https://ipswich.isoplan.com.au/eplan/rules/0/332/0/0/0/203 (JSON: https://ipswich.isoplan.com.au/eplan/api/l/r/332/0/false/30-Jun-2026/false)$q$, $q$Relative setback; needs neighbouring building data.$q$, $q$char_ao7_2_setback_match_character$q$);
SELECT define_rule($q${"rule_id": "ICC.char_ao7_2_setback_match_character", "instrument_version": "ICC_CITY_PLAN_2025@2026-07-01", "topic": "SETBACK.FRONTAGE", "title": "8.2.3.3 Table 8.2.3.3.2 (Benchmarks for Assessable Development), PO7.2 / AO7.2", "role": "REQUIREMENT", "regime": "PLANNING", "enforceability": "DEEMED_TO_COMPLY", "provision_kind": "ACCEPTABLE_OUTCOME", "measurement": "SCHEME_SETBACK_FRONT", "operator": ">=", "value": {"op": "unencoded", "text": "setback >= adjacent character building setback", "extracted_value": null, "extracted_operator": ">="}, "unit": "m", "on_noncompliance": "PLANNING_APPROVAL_REQUIRED", "effective_from": "2026-07-01", "verification": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM", "automatable": false, "scopes": [{"level": "LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "lg": "IPSWICH"}, {"level": "OVERLAY", "overlay": "ICC:OV:OV3_CHARACTER_PLACES_AND_AREAS_OVERLAY"}, {"level": "OVERLAY", "overlay": "ICC:OV:OV3_CHARACTER_PLACES_AND_AREAS_OVERLAY"}], "subjects": ["ANY"], "sources": [{"key": "char_ao7_2_setback_match_character", "role": "PRIMARY"}], "interpretation_notes": "AUTO-IMPORTED (draft). Extracted structure: {\"parameter\": \"street setback\", \"operator\": \">=\", \"value\": null, \"unit\": \"m\", \"conditions\": [\">= setback of adjacent character buildings\", \"not in front of the building alignment of existing character buildings\", \"built to boundary only where adjoining character buildings are\"], \"exceptions\": [\"where no character building for reference, comply with zone outcomes\"], \"formula_text\": \"setback >= adjacent character building setback\"}\nStructure scope 'new buildings and extensions' mapped by keyword to ['ANY'] (default)\nAlternative provision to QDC/QHC: NO\nResearcher notes: Code-assessable development only."}$q$::jsonb);
UPDATE rule_versions SET status = 'DRAFT' WHERE rule_version_id = $q$ICC.char_ao7_2_setback_match_character@2026-07-01$q$;
SELECT define_provision($q$ICC_CITY_PLAN_2025@2026-07-01$q$, $q$8.2.3.3 Table 8.2.3.3.2, PO5.1 / AO5.1$q$, 'PERFORMANCE_OUTCOME', $q$PO5.1
Where the site is situated within a character area or residential setting, buildings are in the range of one to two storeys in height (including single storey high set) with an emphasis placed on elevated buildings on stumps, consistent with the height of adjoining character buildings or the predominant height or rhythm of character buildings within the streetscape or hillscape;
Where the site is situated within a centre or industrial zone or a commercial or industrial setting, buildings are in the range of one to two storeys in height, consistent with the height of adjacent character buildings or the predominant height or rhythm of character buildings within the streetscape or hillscape;
An additional storey is not provided unless appropriate with regard to:
the character and amenity of the area and the overall townscape including hillscapes;
the scale of adjoining development and the predominant height of buildings within the street or hillscape;
the retention of important view corridors; and
the retention of the significance of landmark sites and structures;
Where the site is situated within a commercial or industrial zone, or a commercial or industrial setting, the height of buildings at the street alignment are designed to:
maintain a human scale, particularly at the street level; and
maintain the visual prominence of significant landscape features (including landmark sites) and conserve desirable view corridors; and
New buildings which are situated adjacent to character buildings or character places are designed to ensure that the building is not of a height or bulk to:
visually dominate the character building or character place; or
obstruct views of the character building or character place where visible from a road or the public realm.
AO5.1
No accepted outcome provided.$q$, 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', $q$ruleId 14394$q$, NULL, $q$Character Places and Areas Overlay Code$q$, NULL, $q$https://ipswich.isoplan.com.au/eplan/rules/0/332/0/0/0/203 (JSON: https://ipswich.isoplan.com.au/eplan/api/l/r/332/0/false/30-Jun-2026/false)$q$, $q$$q$, $q$char_po5_1_height_storeys$q$);
